obally; unmatched contexts remain excluded.","sourceHeadwordId":"Jehu","term":"Jehu"}],"matchingRule":"reviewed_exact_headword","matchingRules":["reviewed_exact_headword"],"sourceProvenanceId":"Jehu","sourceTitle":"Jehu"},{"evidence":[{"matchingRule":"reviewed_exact_headword","phrase":"Jerusalem","senseEvidence":{"basis":"reviewed_unambiguous_name","originalCitations":[],"ruleId":"Jerusalem::Jerusalem::reviewed_unambiguous_name","sourceHeadwordId":"Jerusalem"},"text":"When Jehoshaphat king of Judah had returned safely to his home in Jerusalem,","verse":1},{"matchingRule":"reviewed_exact_headword","phrase":"Jerusalem","senseEvidence":{"basis":"reviewed_unambiguous_name","originalCitations":[],"ruleId":"Jerusalem::Jerusalem::reviewed_unambiguous_name","sourceHeadwordId":"Jerusalem"},"text":"Jehoshaphat lived in Jerusalem, and once again he went out among the people from Beersheba to the hill country of Ephraim and turned them back to the LORD, the God of their fathers.","verse":4},{"matchingRule":"reviewed_exact_headword","phrase":"Jerusalem","senseEvidence":{"basis":"reviewed_unambiguous_name","originalCitations":[],"ruleId":"Jerusalem::Jerusalem::reviewed_unambiguous_name","sourceHeadwordId":"Jerusalem"},"text":"Moreover, Jehoshaphat appointed in Jerusalem some of the Levites, priests, and heads of the Israelite families to judge on behalf of the LORD and to settle disputes. And they lived in Jerusalem.","verse":8}],"id":"Jerusalem","label":"Jerusalem","matchReviews":[{"ruleId":"Jerusalem::Jerusalem::reviewed_unambiguous_name","scope":"reviewed_unambiguous_name","senseReview":"Reviewed complete original name headword and source subject. Article covers the biblical person(s), named place, or named spiritual figure denoted by this exact spelling; multiple persons under one unchanged source article remain together. Actual proper-name capitalization and whole-name boundaries required. Explicit occurrence-level ambiguity exclusions override this rule.","sourceHeadwordId":"Jerusalem","term":"Jerusalem"}],"matchingRule":"reviewed_exact_headword","matchingRules":["reviewed_exact_headword"],"sourceProvenanceId":"Jerusalem","sourceTitle":"Jerusalem"},{"evidence":[{"matchingRule":"reviewed_exact_headword","phrase":"LORD","senseEvidence":{"basis":"reviewed_capitalized_divine_title","originalCitations":[],"ruleId":"Lord::LORD::reviewed_capitalized_divine_title","sourceHeadwordId":"Lord"},"text":"Jehu son of Hanani the seer went out to confront him and said to King Jehoshaphat, “Should you help the wicked and love those who hate the LORD? Because of this, the wrath of the LORD is upon you.","verse":2},{"matchingRule":"reviewed_exact_headword","phrase":"LORD","senseEvidence":{"basis":"reviewed_capitalized_divine_title","originalCitations":[],"ruleId":"Lord::LORD::reviewed_capitalized_divine_title","sourceHeadwordId":"Lord"},"text":"Jehoshaphat lived in Jerusalem, and once again he went out among the people from Beersheba to the hill country of Ephraim and turned them back to the LORD, the God of their fathers.","verse":4},{"matchingRule":"reviewed_exact_headword","phrase":"LORD","senseEvidence":{"basis":"reviewed_capitalized_divine_title","originalCitations":[],"ruleId":"Lord::LORD::reviewed_capitalized_divine_title","sourceHeadwordId":"Lord"},"text":"Then he said to the judges, “Consider carefully what you do, for you are not judging for man, but for the LORD, who is with you when you render judgment.","verse":6},{"matchingRule":"reviewed_exact_headword","phrase":"LORD","senseEvidence":{"basis":"reviewed_capitalized_divine_title","originalCitations":[],"ruleId":"Lord::LORD::reviewed_capitalized_divine_title","sourceHeadwordId":"Lord"},"text":"And now, may the fear of the LORD be upon you. Be careful what you do, for with the LORD our God there is no injustice or partiality or bribery.”","verse":7},{"matchingRule":"reviewed_exact_headword","phrase":"LORD","senseEvidence":{"basis":"reviewed_capitalized_divine_title","originalCitations":[],"ruleId":"Lord::LORD::reviewed_capitalized_divine_title","sourceHeadwordId":"Lord"},"text":"Moreover, Jehoshaphat appointed in Jerusalem some of the Levites, priests, and heads of the Israelite families to judge on behalf of the LORD and to settle disputes. And they lived in Jerusalem.","verse":8},{"matchingRule":"reviewed_exact_headword","phrase":"LORD","senseEvidence":{"basis":"reviewed_capitalized_divine_title","originalCitations":[],"ruleId":"Lord::LORD::reviewed_capitalized_divine_title","sourceHeadwordId":"Lord"},"text":"He commanded them, saying, “You must serve faithfully and wholeheartedly in the fear of the LORD.","verse":9},{"matchingRule":"reviewed_exact_headword","phrase":"LORD","senseEvidence":{"basis":"reviewed_capitalized_divine_title","originalCitations":[],"ruleId":"Lord::LORD::reviewed_capitalized_divine_title","sourceHeadwordId":"Lord"},"text":"For every dispute that comes before you from your brothers who dwell in their cities—whether it regards bloodshed or some other violation of law, commandments, statutes, or ordinances—you are to warn them, so that they will not incur guilt before the LORD and wrath will not come upon you and your brothers. Do this, and you will not incur guilt.","verse":10},{"matchingRule":"reviewed_exact_headword","phrase":"LORD","senseEvidence":{"basis":"reviewed_capitalized_divine_title","originalCitations":[],"ruleId":"Lord::LORD::reviewed_capitalized_divine_title","sourceHeadwordId":"Lord"},"text":"Note that Amariah, the chief priest, will be over you in all that pertains to the LORD, and Zebadiah son of Ishmael, the ruler of the house of Judah, in all that pertains to the king. And the Levites will serve as officers before you. Act resolutely; may the LORD be with the upright!”","verse":11}],"id":"Lord","label":"LORD","matchReviews":[{"ruleId":"Lord::LORD::reviewed_capitalized_divine_title","scope":"reviewed_capitalized_divine_title","senseReview":"Only literal uppercase LORD is admitted globally. Source Lord article explicitly covers God as Lord; lowercase human lord and sentence-title Lord are not inferred from this rule.","sourceHeadwordId":"Lord","term":"LORD"}],"matchingRule":"reviewed_exact_headword","matchingRules":["reviewed_exact_headword"],"sourceProvenanceId":"Lord","sourceTitle":"Lord"}],"format":"bsb-study-chapter-v2","notes":[{"chapterAssociationStatus":"canonical_reference","content":[{"c":["Jehoshaphat"],"sourceClass":"profile-title","t":"h"},{"c":["Jehoshaphat succeeded his father Asa to become the fourth king of Judah (872–848 ",{"c":["BC"],"sourceClass":"era","t":"span"},"). Like Hezekiah and Josiah after him, Jehoshaphat trusted the Lord throughout his life and worked to remove most forms of pagan worship from Israel (",{"href":"?bref=2Chr.17.6","r":"2Chr.17.6","rawR":"2Chr.17.6","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"2Chr.17.6","value":"2Chr.17.6"}],"t":"ref","v":"2 Chr 17:6"},")."],"sourceClass":"profile-body-fl","t":"p"},{"c":["Jehoshaphat continued his father Asa’s religious reforms but reversed his foreign policy. Jehoshaphat discontinued Judah’s war with Israel over their boundaries (see ",{"href":"?bref=1Kgs.22.2","r":"1Kgs.22.2","rawR":"1Kgs.22.2","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"1Kgs.22.2","value":"1Kgs.22.2"}],"t":"ref","v":"1 Kgs 22:2"},") and made an alliance with Ahab. To confirm this alliance, he arranged for his son Jehoram to marry Ahab’s daughter Athaliah (",{"href":"?bref=2Chr.18.1-2","r":"2Chr.18.1-2","rawR":"2Chr.18.1-2","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"2Chr.18.1-2","value":"2Chr.18.1-2"}],"t":"ref","v":"2 Chr 18:1-2"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=2Kgs.8.18","r":"2Kgs.8.18","rawR":"2Kgs.8.18","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"2Kgs.8.18","value":"2Kgs.8.18"}],"t":"ref","v":"2 Kgs 8:18"},") and supported the north in its wars against the Arameans and Moabites (",{"href":"?bref=2Chr.18.3-34","r":"2Chr.18.3-34","rawR":"2Chr.18.3-34","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"2Chr.18.3-34","value":"2Chr.18.3-34"}],"t":"ref","v":"2 Chr 18:3-34"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=1Kgs.22.1-53","r":"1Kgs.22.1-53","rawR":"1Kgs.22.1-53","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"1Kgs.22.1-53","value":"1Kgs.22.1-53"}],"t":"ref","v":"1 Kgs 22"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=2Kgs.3.4-27","r":"2Kgs.3.4-27","rawR":"2Kgs.3.4-27","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"2Kgs.3.4-27","value":"2Kgs.3.4-27"}],"t":"ref","v":"2 Kgs 3:4-27"},"). The prophet Jehu rebuked Jehoshaphat for his unwise alliance with Israel (",{"href":"?bref=2Chr.19.1-3","r":"2Chr.19.1-3","rawR":"2Chr.19.1-3","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"2Chr.19.1-3","value":"2Chr.19.1-3"}],"t":"ref","v":"2 Chr 19:1-3"},"), which resulted in his son Jehoram falling under the influence of Ahab and Jezebel. Jehoram and his son Ahaziah turned Judah toward idol worship."],"sourceClass":"profile-body","t":"p"},{"c":["Yet during his reign, Jehoshaphat kept the worship of the Lord pure. He closed the temples of prostitution (",{"href":"?bref=1Kgs.22.46","r":"1Kgs.22.46","rawR":"1Kgs.22.46","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"1Kgs.22.46","value":"1Kgs.22.46"}],"t":"ref","v":"1 Kgs 22:46"},") and sent teachers of God’s law throughout the land (",{"href":"?bref=2Chr.17.7-9","r":"2Chr.17.7-9","rawR":"2Chr.17.7-9","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"2Chr.17.7-9","value":"2Chr.17.7-9"}],"t":"ref","v":"2 Chr 17:7-9"},"). He also established a system of judges and admonished them to function as the Lord’s representatives so that justice might prevail (",{"href":"?bref=2Chr.19.4-7","r":"2Chr.19.4-7","rawR":"2Chr.19.4-7","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"2Chr.19.4-7","value":"2Chr.19.4-7"}],"t":"ref","v":"19:4-7"},"). He appointed Levites, priests, and family heads to handle cases pertaining to religious practice and to negotiate disputes among citizens (",{"href":"?bref=2Chr.19.8-10","r":"2Chr.19.8-10","rawR":"2Chr.19.8-10","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"2Chr.19.8-10","value":"2Chr.19.8-10"}],"t":"ref","v":"19:8-10"},")."],"sourceClass":"profile-body","t":"p"},{"c":["Before going to battle, Jehoshaphat would insist on hearing from a true prophet of the Lord. And in one of the most stirring descriptions of war in the Old Testament, Jehoshaphat preached to the army before entering a battle. As a result, God caused the armies from Ammon, Moab, and their allies to turn against each other (",{"href":"?bref=2Chr.20.1-37","r":"2Chr.20.1-37","rawR":"2Chr.20.1-37","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"2Chr.20.1-37","value":"2Chr.20.1-37"}],"t":"ref","v":"2 Chr 20"},")."],"sourceClass":"profile-body","t":"p"},{"c":["Jehoshaphat died when he was about sixty years old and was buried in Jerusalem. His son Jehoram became Judah’s next king (",{"href":"?bref=2Chr.21.1","r":"2Chr.21.1","rawR":"2Chr.21.1","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"2Chr.21.1","value":"2Chr.21.1"}],"t":"ref","v":"21:1"},")."],"sourceClass":"profile-body","t":"p"},{"c":["Passages for Further Study"],"sourceClass":"profile-refs-title","t":"h"},{"c":[{"href":"?bref=1Kgs.15.24","r":"1Kgs.15.24","rawR":"1Kgs.15.24","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"1Kgs.15.24","value":"1Kgs.15.24"}],"t":"ref","v":"1 Kgs 15:24"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=1Kgs.22.1-50","r":"1Kgs.22.1-50","rawR":"1Kgs.22.1-50","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"1Kgs.22.1-50","value":"1Kgs.22.1-50"}],"t":"ref","v":"22:1-50"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=2Kgs.3.1-27","r":"2Kgs.3.1-27","rawR":"2Kgs.3.1-27","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"2Kgs.3.1-27","value":"2Kgs.3.1-27"}],"t":"ref","v":"2 Kgs 3:1-27"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=2Chr.17.1-21","r":"2Chr.17.1-21","rawR":"2Chr.17.1-21","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"2Chr.17.1-21","value":"2Chr.17.1-21"}],"t":"ref","v":"2 Chr 17:1–21:1"}],"sourceClass":"profile-refs","t":"p"}],"id":"Profile:Jehoshaphat","refs":[{"book":"2CH","endChapter":21,"endVerse":2,"startChapter":17,"startVerse":1}],"sourceAttributes":{"name":"Jehoshaphat","product":"TyndaleOpenStudyNotes","typename":"Profile"},"sourceBookAppCode":"2CH","sourceChapterCoverage":[17,18,19,20,21],"sourceItemFragmentSha256":"4f346bc89e30a1c599aafc8ad25c1d1284fb1eed94055941ce5f3dabccd4307c","sourceItemName":"Jehoshaphat","sourceMember":"Tyndale Open Study Notes/Profiles.xml","sourceOrder":62,"sourceReferenceException":false,"sourceReferenceMappingEvidence":{"appCode":"2CH","canonicalOSIS":"2Chr","method":"official_book_intro_ref_title","sourceOSIS":"2Chr"},"sourceReferenceStatus":"canonical","sourceRefsExact":"2Chr.17.1-21.2","sourceRelease":"1.25","sourceTitleExact":"Jehoshaphat","supplementPointersNotIncludedAsContent":[],"title":"Jehoshaphat","type":"Profile"},{"chapterAssociationStatus":"canonical_reference","content":[{"c":[{"c":[{"href":"?bref=2Chr.19.1-2","r":"2Chr.19.1-2","rawR":"2Chr.19.1-2","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"2Chr.19.1-2","value":"2Chr.19.1-2"}],"t":"ref","v":"19:1-2"}],"sourceClass":"sn-ref","t":"span"}," ",{"c":["Jehu"],"sourceClass":"sn-excerpt","t":"span"}," was the ",{"c":["son of Hanani,"],"sourceClass":"sn-excerpt","t":"span"}," the prophet who had rebuked Asa for his reliance on the Arameans (",{"href":"?bref=2Chr.16.7-9","r":"2Chr.16.7-9","rawR":"2Chr.16.7-9","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"2Chr.16.7-9","value":"2Chr.16.7-9"}],"t":"ref","v":"16:7-9"},"). Jehu now chastised Jehoshaphat for his alliance with Ahab. • The word ",{"c":["love"],"sourceClass":"sn-excerpt","t":"span"}," expresses faithfulness to a covenant. Jehoshaphat’s covenant with ",{"c":["the wicked"],"sourceClass":"sn-excerpt","t":"span"}," Ahab conflicted with his covenant with the Lord."],"sourceClass":"sn-text","t":"p"}],"id":"StudyNote:IIChr.19.1-2","refs":[{"book":"2CH","endChapter":19,"endVerse":2,"startChapter":19,"startVerse":1}],"sourceAttributes":{"name":"IIChr.19.1-2","product":"TyndaleOpenStudyNotes","typename":"StudyNote"},"sourceBookAppCode":"2CH","sourceChapterCoverage":[19],"sourceItemFragmentSha256":"2cb30f7c38a1a92b2f577161c571a1db2e48bb95eb8e8c5c832dc2af7329f0cd","sourceItemName":"IIChr.19.1-2","sourceMember":"Tyndale Open Study Notes/StudyNotes.xml","sourceOrder":5031,"sourceReferenceException":false,"sourceReferenceMappingEvidence":{"appCode":"2CH","canonicalOSIS":"2Chr","method":"official_book_intro_ref_title","sourceOSIS":"2Chr"},"sourceReferenceStatus":"canonical","sourceRefsExact":"2Chr.19.1-2","sourceRelease":"1.25","sourceTitleExact":null,"supplementPointersNotIncludedAsContent":[],"title":"IIChr.19.1-2","type":"StudyNote"},{"chapterAssociationStatus":"canonical_reference","content":[{"c":[{"c":[{"href":"?bref=2Chr.19.4-11","r":"2Chr.19.4-11","rawR":"2Chr.19.4-11","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"2Chr.19.4-11","value":"2Chr.19.4-11"}],"t":"ref","v":"19:4-11"}],"sourceClass":"sn-ref","t":"span"}," In Jehoshaphat’s judicial reform, he appointed ",{"c":["judges"],"sourceClass":"sn-excerpt","t":"span"}," in the ",{"c":["fortified towns"],"sourceClass":"sn-excerpt","t":"span"}," (",{"href":"?bref=2Chr.19.5","r":"2Chr.19.5","rawR":"2Chr.19.5","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"2Chr.19.5","value":"2Chr.19.5"}],"t":"ref","v":"19:5"},") and in a central court ",{"c":["in Jerusalem"],"sourceClass":"sn-excerpt","t":"span"}," (",{"href":"?bref=2Chr.19.8","r":"2Chr.19.8","rawR":"2Chr.19.8","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"2Chr.19.8","value":"2Chr.19.8"}],"t":"ref","v":"19:8"},"). He exhorted all the judges to ",{"c":["think carefully"],"sourceClass":"sn-excerpt","t":"span"},{"c":[","],"sourceClass":"ital","t":"span"}," and to ",{"c":["judge with integrity"],"sourceClass":"sn-excerpt","t":"span"}," and ",{"c":["in the fear of the"],"sourceClass":"sn-excerpt","t":"span"}," ",{"c":["Lord"],"sourceClass":"sn-excerpt-divine-name","t":"span"},". This excluded acting with any ",{"c":["partiality"],"sourceClass":"sn-excerpt","t":"span"}," or ",{"c":["taking of bribes"],"sourceClass":"sn-excerpt","t":"span"},{"c":[","],"sourceClass":"ital","t":"span"}," and included warning criminals ",{"c":["not to sin against the"],"sourceClass":"sn-excerpt","t":"span"}," ",{"c":["Lord"],"sourceClass":"sn-excerpt-divine-name","t":"span"},". The reform reestablished the law of Deuteronomy (",{"href":"?bref=Deut.16.18-17.13","r":"Deut.16.18-17.13","rawR":"Deut.16.18-17.13","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Deut.16.18-17.13","value":"Deut.16.18-17.13"}],"t":"ref","v":"Deut 16:18–17:13"},")."],"sourceClass":"sn-text","t":"p"}],"id":"StudyNote:IIChr.19.4-11","refs":[{"book":"2CH","endChapter":19,"endVerse":11,"startChapter":19,"startVerse":4}],"sourceAttributes":{"name":"IIChr.19.4-11","product":"TyndaleOpenStudyNotes","typename":"StudyNote"},"sourceBookAppCode":"2CH","sourceChapterCoverage":[19],"sourceItemFragmentSha256":"4a8dd0ffa331fb1a08bd350fa94ef4f93b13669d0183d3e02108e8ec9a21357a","sourceItemName":"IIChr.19.4-11","sourceMember":"Tyndale Open Study Notes/StudyNotes.xml","sourceOrder":5032,"sourceReferenceException":false,"sourceReferenceMappingEvidence":{"appCode":"2CH","canonicalOSIS":"2Chr","method":"official_book_intro_ref_title","sourceOSIS":"2Chr"},"sourceReferenceStatus":"canonical","sourceRefsExact":"2Chr.19.4-11","sourceRelease":"1.25","sourceTitleExact":null,"supplementPointersNotIncludedAsContent":[],"title":"IIChr.19.4-11","type":"StudyNote"}],"version":"v2-a101d843a2f0cd3fc0c6"}